      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "lem-knot-connected-sum-well-defined-step-1-1",
          "claim": "1.1 A change of knot representative already comes with an oriented ambient isotopy by [F1]. Applying that isotopy to its ball-arc data carries the cut complement and its boundary collars to the new data, so the standard gluing produces an ambient-isotopic sum. A change of radius in one local straightening chart is the isotopy that rescales the standard ball radially while preserving its oriented diameter. This is an isotopy of compact ball-arc embeddings, so [A1] and [F3] extend it to an ambient isotopy of the knot sphere.",
