          "id": "lem-knot-connected-sum-well-defined-step-1-2",
          "claim": "1.2 For two local oriented ball-arc charts centered at the same point, express them in one smooth coordinate chart. Their transition germ fixes the center, carries the positive tangent line of the knot to itself, and has positive determinant. Shrink to a common ball and use the smooth rescaling homotopy $G_s(x)=s^{-1}(G(sx)-G(0))$ for $s>0$, with $G_0(x)=DG_0(x)$. Taylor's formula gives the smooth extension at $s=0$. On a sufficiently small common ball the differentials stay uniformly close to the injective linear map $DG_0$, so every $G_s$ is an embedding and preserves the oriented diameter. The subgroup of invertible linear maps preserving that oriented line and the ambient orientation is path-connected: in line-normal coordinates its diagonal blocks lie in $(0,\\infty)$ and $GL^+(2,\\mathbb R)$, and the shear block contracts linearly to zero. Thus the chart germ is isotopic through oriented ball-arc embeddings to the fixed standard chart.",
